# Dev-time API target — Expo loads this automatically on `expo start`.
#
# Leave it EMPTY. The Expo dev server proxies /api/* to the gateway (see
# metro.config.js), so the API is served from the same origin as the JS bundle
# and the app resolves that origin at runtime (see index.js). Browser, emulator,
# and a phone on `--tunnel` all reach the backend with nothing to configure.
#
# Set it only to pin the app at a specific gateway — that overrides the
# auto-detection. API_PROXY_TARGET changes where the proxy forwards to
# (default http://localhost:3001), which is the better knob when the backend is
# just running somewhere else locally.
#
# EAS builds ignore this file and use the env block in eas.json instead.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=
